From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:35:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dp: the console takes a DisplayPort connector
 without the Dolby Vision tunnel

linux-9977 attaches DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB to the DisplayPort connector
of a port with a DisplayPort to HDMI converter, but intel_dp_connector_funcs
has no atomic_client_restore (linux-9958). When the in-kernel client takes
the display back (Kodi stopped, or killed while it played Dolby Vision
through the converter), its commit kept the tunnel on: the scanout of the
console passes the checks of the tunnel (one XRGB8888 plane, full screen,
no colour processing), so the console went out with the Dolby VSIF, which
the display reads as Dolby Vision, and the property stayed set for the
next start of Kodi.

The DisplayPort connector now has the hook of the HDMI one
(intel_digital_connector_client_restore()): the tunnel, Low-Latency, the
HDMI 1.4b signal, HDR over the tunnel and the HDR10 depth guard go off in
the console's commit, which makes it a full modeset. A DisplayPort
connector without these properties has them all off: nothing changes
there, eDP included.

Host test: each drm_connector_funcs of the files of i915 that make
DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB (intel_hdmi.c, intel_dp.c) has the hook; it fails
without this change. W=1 on i915 and xe: no warning. Not run on hardware.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
index fa483b02d..560edf438 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
@@ -7117,6 +7117,11 @@ static const struct drm_connector_funcs intel_dp_connector_funcs = {
 	.atomic_destroy_state = drm_atomic_helper_connector_destroy_state,
 	.atomic_duplicate_state = intel_digital_connector_duplicate_state,
 	.oob_hotplug_event = intel_dp_oob_hotplug_event,
+	/*
+	 * Hades: no Dolby Vision tunnel left on for the console, through the DisplayPort to HDMI
+	 * converter of a board either (intel_dp_pcon_dv_add_properties())
+	 */
+	.atomic_client_restore = intel_digital_connector_client_restore,
 };
 
 static const struct drm_connector_helper_funcs intel_dp_connector_helper_funcs = {
-- 
